close_range: clamp the closed range to the descriptor table.

The backported __close_range() kept the 6.x punch_hole/dup_fd structure
but lost upstream's clamp of max_fd to the fdtable. close_range(3, ~0U, 0),
used by systemd/elogind safe_fork(), then calls pick_file() for ~2^31
descriptors and spins for about 30 seconds in the kernel, delaying every
elogind fork (backlight SetBrightness, sleep). Clamp as upstream does.

--- a/fs/file.c
+++ b/fs/file.c
@@ -705,6 +705,14 @@
 static inline void __range_close(struct files_struct *cur_fds, unsigned int fd,
 				 unsigned int max_fd)
 {
+	unsigned int n;
+
+	/* Like upstream, never walk past the descriptor table. */
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	n = last_fd(files_fdtable(cur_fds));
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+	max_fd = min(max_fd, n);
+
